{"PASSING_NPC_GREET","reg=law|tmp=seasoned,veteran",{"I haven't heard from dispatch in days","I used to write parking tickets, now I write names of the dead","Don't use the radio, it just draws attention","Half the department's gone, the other half's tired","Haven't slept right since the ninth, you?","How many have we lost? I stopped counting","Anybody knows what's going on at the courthouse? I heard shouting","Used to know every face in this county, now I know their names on the wall","Day {day}, still no word from state, you believe that?","I think we're all just waiting for somebody to tell us to stop","Sometimes I forget what a quiet shift felt like"}},
