{"PASSING_NPC_GREET","reg=civilian|tmp=seasoned",{"You see anything I should know? No? Good","Found a can of peaches yesterday, felt like Christmas","Didn't see you, you didn't see me, fine by me","Dogs have gotten bold around here, just so you know","I check every house on this side, nothing left, don't waste your time","Don't bother with the gas station, I got there first","Seen the old man in the yellow house? He stopped waving","Any of you handy with a rifle? Just asking","Safe to talk? Okay, then, how's the east side?","You hear anything good? Anything? I'll take a rumor","I've got a place on the hill, it's quiet, if you need to know","Don't trust anybody who's too friendly, present company excepted","I keep a count of the ones I put down, I'm at fourteen, you?","I'd walk around the next block, there's a pack of dogs by the school","Found a stream out back of the lot, it's clean, as far as I can tell","Trade you a pack of batteries for something with caffeine","You'd be amazed what people leave in their glove boxes","There's a church that still takes people in, if you need it","I counted seven bodies on Elm, and I'm not going back","Last guy I talked to wanted my shoes, so, forgive me if I'm tense","Don't wave, they notice waving","You can pass, but shh, I'm trying to hear","Careful on the left side, there's glass, I learned that with my foot","You wouldn't happen to have a lighter? I'd trade a can of corn","Lost my map in the creek, so, I'm walking by feel","You carrying much? I used to carry thirty pounds, now it's twelve","I don't talk much, but I'm listening","Trade you a can of green beans for a clean sock","You know how to gut a squirrel? I'm learning, it's not pretty","Don't whistle out here, it carries","If you hear a bell, that's the church, not the dead, probably"}},
{"PASSING_NPC_GREET","reg=civilian|tmp=seasoned|world=door",{"Little place on Pine, door's open, nobody's home, have at it","Know anywhere I can sleep without a door? It's a long story"}},
{"PASSING_NPC_GREET","reg=civilian|day=0,4",{"Did you hear? It's on the radio, it's everywhere","Is it true about the bridge? That they closed the bridge?","Stay away from Main, it's bad, there's people just- attacking people","Hey! Are you bit? Is anybody bit? Let me see!","Where are you headed? We're going to the school, they said buses","Don't go home, whatever you do, don't go home","My neighbor tried to eat his wife, I'm not kidding, I saw it","I called the county office and just got a busy signal","Have you got any news? Anything? Anything?","They said it's rabies, but I don't believe it, do you?","Everybody's running, where is everybody running to?","They're saying stay inside, but inside isn't safe either","Did you see the helicopters? The Army's coming, right? Right?","It's like a movie, but it's not, God, it's not"}},
{"PASSING_NPC_GREET","reg=family",{"Keep up, kids. Say hello, then we're moving","Hello, neighbor, everything alright at your house?","Y'all need anything? We've got extra beans, not much else","We've got a pot of soup going back home, if you pass by","Hello. Careful, the kids are cranky today","Hi there, don't mind the baby, she's fussy","We heard a noise from your house yesterday, you okay?","We're all fine, thanks, just a little hungry","Hi, have you seen a station wagon with a dent? My brother's driving it","Are y'all going to the church? We heard there's food","Do you need to borrow a hammer? We've got extra","Papaw says hi, he doesn't say much else anymore","It's good to see another family, honestly","Oh, you've got kids, too, they can play, there's nobody else","Don't wander off, kids, stay where I can see you","You folks look tired, sit a while if you want","We're headed to my mother's, she's in Rosewood, any idea if it's safe?","Mind the kids, they spook easy","How's your mama and them? I was thinking about her the other day","We've got two spare blankets, if you need","Did you hear anything about the school? My boy's teacher is there","You've got a good-looking family, God bless 'em","Our dog's missing, answers to Biscuit, hasn't been home since Friday","Sorry for staring, we haven't seen a family in days","Y'all got kids? Ours could use somebody to play with","We've got a pot of beans going, plenty if you're hungry","Hi, we're the Parkers, out on Ridge Road","We were at the church, but it's full, so we're heading to my sister's","Mind the little one, he runs toward everything","Any word on the school? My daughter's teacher is there, I think","Our truck's out of gas, so, we're walking, don't ask","We're a big family, it's loud, don't mind us","Anybody seen a boy in a Wildcats shirt? He's ten, he wanders off","Do you need a place to sleep? We've got a floor, it's not much","Kids, wave. Slowly, let them see your hands","We heard shots by the water tower, so we're going around","We brought a wagon, it's slow, but it carries the baby","That's a nice dog, ours ran off, Friday","Papaw's tired, so we're resting here, if you don't mind","We left the house on Tuesday, and it's the saddest thing I've ever done","I'm so glad you're not alone, the kids needed to see that","Kids, hold hands, we're crossing here","Y'all got room in that wagon? Our baby's tired","Say hi, sweetie, they're nice, they're not scary","You're going the same way we are, mind if we follow?","Do you know a place with a bathroom? Don't laugh, a real one","Our dog's friendly, he just smells bad, sorry","Hello, everybody, how are the children?","We'd stop and chat, but the baby needs changing, goodbye","Good to see folks sticking together, it makes me hopeful","We're staying at the Lutheran church, if you need a place","Yes, the red wagon's ours, no, it's not for sale","We're the Tanners, from out on Hardin Springs Road, did you know the Tanners?","Do you have any extra shoes? The little one's grown out of everything","We just had a birthday, can you believe it? Seven years old","Can you spare a match? We're trying to get a fire going, and it's damp","I miss Sunday dinners, you know, the whole table full","Anybody seen a cat? Gray, missing an ear, answers to Pickle","My son wants to know if you're a soldier, I told him no","My mother-in-law says hello, she says it's the end times, I say it's Tuesday","The baby's first word was 'dog', so, that's something good","Papaw taught the boys to fish, and now it's the only skill that matters","Are you headed to the Baptist church? We heard there's a kitchen"}},
